Cc: justicecom@parliament.uk; HLAutismAct2009@parliament.uk
Subject: AC-2025-LON-004293 =E2=80=94 Zahmoul v Secretary of State for Justice & =
Ors =E2=80=94 Filing of Reconsideration Submission & Transparency Notice
Importance: High

=20

Dear Administrative Court Office,
Dear Secretary of State for Justice,
Dear Chair, Justice Committee,
Dear Chair, Autism Act Committee,

I write as the Claimant in Zahmoul v Secretary of State for Justice & HMCTS=
 (Administrative Court reference AC-2025-LON-004293).

Further to the Court=E2=80=99s Order dated 4 December 2025, I have today filed my=
 Reconsideration Submission and supporting materials. The submission respond=
s directly to the three issues identified in the Order and places before the=
 Court the relevant statutory duties under the Autism Act 2009, Equality Act=
 2010, the Public Sector Equality Duty, and the findings of the House of Lor=
ds Select Committee on the Autism Act in its recent report Time to Deliver (=
HL Paper 205, 23 November 2025).

The Committee=E2=80=99s report identifies systemic deficiencies in accountability=
, safeguarding, and mechanisms for autistic people to raise and escalate con=
cerns. These same deficiencies are directly engaged in this Judicial Review,=
 which concerns the ongoing failure to maintain participation measures for a=
utism and PTSD, the absence of any equality-compliant adjustments, and the s=
ystemic non-engagement with repeated safeguarding disclosures.

Because I am an autistic, vulnerable person with PTSD, a serious chronic au=
to-immune disorder, complex co-occurring mental health difficulties, and I a=
m unrepresented,  in order to ensure transparency, continuity, truth, and ac=
curacy in these proceedings, I have created a public, immutable, timestamped=
 repository containing all the official documents and evidence related to th=
is Judicial Review and underlying court proceedings, updated on a daily basi=
s.

Public Repository (official documents):

https://github.com/nadiazahmoul/JR-Zahmoul-v-SSJ-HMCTS-Archive

Filed today with the Administrative Court:
Reconsideration Submission and Appendix (House of Lords Summary Report)
Skeleton Argument
Safeguarding Annex
Exhibit Pack (E31=E2=80=93E40), including participation-failure correspondence, P=
AP and escalation materials, medical and autism evidence.
=20

Kind regards,
Nadia Zahmoul
Claimant (Litigant in Person)
AC-2025-LON-004293
Public Repository (official documents):

https://github.com/nadiazahmoul/JR-Zahmoul-v-SSJ-HMCTS-Archive

=20

